# Who gets asked to review what.
#
# GitHub matches the LAST rule that applies to a file, so the specific rules
# live below the catch-all. Ownership here is a routing table, not a fence: a
# pull request from anyone is welcome on any of these paths.

*                       @GriffinCanCode

# The engine tiers and the contract that binds them. A change to the import
# topology is an architecture change even when the diff is three lines.
/src/                   @GriffinCanCode
/contract/              @GriffinCanCode

# The C ABI is the promise every binding and every face rests on, and it
# freezes at 1.0.0. A header change is an ecosystem change.
/include/               @GriffinCanCode

# Third-party bytes and the attribution that has to travel with them. Never
# edit one of these without the other.
/vendor/                @GriffinCanCode
/NOTICE                 @GriffinCanCode
/LICENSE                @GriffinCanCode

# The measurement apparatus and the dossiers that make a claim falsifiable.
/bench/                 @GriffinCanCode
/research/              @GriffinCanCode

# Anything that can change what CI proves, including this file.
/.github/               @GriffinCanCode
/quality/               @GriffinCanCode
